creature-cli (2.53.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Speak the neutral Creature Server JSON contract from server 3.45.0
    (creature-server#170): absent optionals are omitted rather than sent
    as null, and no field the server doesn't define goes out (console#87,
    superseding #83, #84, and #85).
  * Animation metadata decodes payloads with 'note' omitted, and no longer
    sends 'last_updated' -- a field the server never had, which the new
    codec rejects outright. Saving or renaming an animation works again
    against 3.45.0.
  * Animation metadata now carries 'render_seed', 'source_stage_placements',
    and 'source_render_choices', so renaming a stage- or dialog-rendered
    animation stops silently stripping its provenance.
  * A track has exactly one owner: 'creatures detail' and every other
    animation read now handles fixture-only tracks, which previously failed
    to decode because the server omits 'creature_id' for them.
  * Creature configs model 'mouth_input' and 'gaze'; 'creatures detail'
    prints both.
  * New 'creatures import' command uploads a creature configuration file
    verbatim, with '--register' to also claim a universe. The bytes go up
    unchanged so fields this build doesn't model survive the trip.
  * Playlist item weights are validated against the server's 1-999 range
    before a request is issued.
  * A dialog turn's equality no longer counts its client-only id, which is
    minted fresh on every decode. Comparing turns reported a difference on
    every server round trip, which left the dialog editor permanently
    marked as having unsaved changes after a save.

