 -- April White <april@creature.engineering>  Fri, 25 Jul 2026 02:45:00 -0700

creature-cli (2.42.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * No CLI changes — lockstep bump with the Console app: joystick input is
    now fully event-driven (issue #56). The OS pushes hardware changes
    (IOKit HID callbacks, GameController value-changed handlers) into a
    lock-protected state mirror, and the 50Hz event loop samples that
    mirror directly — no more per-tick main-actor hop, so dragging a color
    wheel (or any main-thread-heavy UI work) can no longer starve the
    robot control cadence. Also stops the first startup tick's ~900ms
    initialization cost from seeding the status bar with a huge negative
    spare-time number.

